* BYEDRIV - BYE DRIVER SUPPORT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* BYEDRIV - BYE DRIVER SUPPORT

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    A0:BYEDRIV

Private driver/support loader used by the installed BYE service. It is not
the caller logoff command and is not intended for direct invocation during
a session.

Retain its matched driver/configuration files and original attributes. Use
public BYE to log off, AUTH for policy inspection in private sysop mode,
and the host launcher for normal startup.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
